# Rust build artifacts — never committed (Stage 69 ships the crate SKELETON only:
# no compiled output, no lockfile, no WASM). A real build/lockfile/manifest lands
# only in a future, explicitly-reviewed stage.
/target/
/build/
Cargo.lock
*.wasm
*.rlib

# WASM generation output (Stage 451, docs/runtime_wasm_generation.md) — the fixed
# `wasm-bindgen --out-dir` destination a future, separate stage would write real
# generated `.wasm`/JS glue/`.d.ts` files into. Nothing is generated by this stage;
# this pattern exists so that IF a future stage ever runs `npm run build:wasm`
# (package.json, Stage 450), its output is never accidentally staged or committed.
/pkg/
